  "oracle_attribution": "The new test case 'zones' calls heapmem_zone_register(...), heapmem_zone_alloc(zone, ...) and references the macros HEAPMEM_ZONE_INVALID/HEAPMEM_ZONE_GENERAL. None of these symbols exist in os/lib/heapmem.{c,h} at base (confirmed: base heapmem.h has only heapmem_alloc/realloc/free; base heapmem.c has only heapmem_alloc). The PR's production diff in os/lib/heapmem.{c,h} introduces exactly this zone API, which is the PR's stated purpose ('dedicated divisions of the heap memory'). The compile failure of the test translation unit is therefore attributable to the very interface the fix supplies, not to an incidental helper, qualifying a semantic compile oracle.",
